# Remote database first

Neon, the database behind franco-may.com, is the source of truth. The admin and the phone read it.

A change that exists only in a local sqlite, jsonl, or `franco-may/data/place-coords.txt.gz` is not done. Write it to the remote table the admin already reads. The pipeline pulls those tables down when it runs and refreshes the local copy from them.

Place coordinates are the example. The live admin shows a pin from `fl_pin_overrides`, then from the deployed coords file. A coordinate written only into the local gzip does not appear.
